From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hayaksi1 <193020925+hayaksi1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 20:19:56 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Give the relocated tests the environment and packages they
 need

Three of them needed a DOM. apps/web defaults to environment: "node", and
a file opts in with a per-file pragma; without it, query.test.ts and
spoiler.test.ts reached FileBodyViewModel's module-level cacheDownloadIcon,
whose window.btoa call rejected during module init rather than inside a
test - killing the worker thread outright. Files a dead worker was running
appear in neither the passed nor the failed tally, so the run looked
coherent while two files silently evaporated.

Four more imported jest-matrix-react, which the vitest migration removed;
they use test-utils-rtl like every other co-located suite. Two imported
mocked from jest-mock without using it, and one reached for SdkContextClass
in SDKContext, where only the React context lives.

Also imports the hooks two files actually use: adding a vitest import that
omits the hook the file calls fixes nothing.

Fork-Feature: fork-tooling
